      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Quincy, Missouri & Pacific Railroad made Novinger a central stop, bringing workers from Wales, Germany, and Italy during the coal boom.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityofnovinger.com/novinger-history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The last deep‑shaft mine in Missouri, Billy Creek, closed in January 1966, ending Novinger’s coal‑mining era.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Novinger%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A 2008 EF2 tornado struck Novinger’s southern edge, damaging over fifty homes but leaving only minor injuries.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
        23,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Novinger%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Flash floods from the Chariton River in 2008 and 2009 repeatedly damaged the historic log homestead and community center.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Novinger%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Today Novinger hosts a reconstructed historic log homestead and the Novinger Coal Miners’ Museum, preserving its mining heritage.",
